# Code Quality Rules
Rule Type: Always

## Trading Strategy Requirements
### Required Methods
- `__init__`: Strategy initialization
- `calculate_indicators`: Technical indicator calculations
- `generate_signals`: Trading signal generation
- `execute_trade`: Trade execution
- `backtest`: Strategy backtesting

### Required Attributes
- `name`: Strategy identifier
- `risk_per_trade`: Maximum risk per trade
- `stop_loss_pct`: Stop loss percentage
- `target_pct`: Target profit percentage

### Error Handling
- Wrap all trading operations in try-except
- Log all errors with appropriate severity
- Implement proper error recovery
- Handle market data errors
- Manage connection failures

### Logging
- Use logger instead of print
- Log all trade executions
- Log all signal generations
- Log all errors with stack traces
- Include context in log messages

## IBKR Connection Requirements
### Required Methods
- `connect`: Establish connection
- `disconnect`: Close connection
- `place_order`: Submit trade orders
- `cancel_order`: Cancel pending orders
- `get_order_status`: Check order status

### Error Handling
- Handle connection failures
- Handle order placement failures
- Implement reconnection logic
- Manage session timeouts
- Handle market data errors

### Logging
- Log all connection events
- Log all order operations
- Log all errors with stack traces
- Include order details in logs
- Track connection state

## General Code Quality
### Code Organization
- Follow single responsibility principle
- Keep methods focused and small
- Use meaningful variable names
- Document complex logic
- Maintain clean code structure

### Performance
- Optimize critical paths
- Minimize memory usage
- Reduce network calls
- Cache frequently used data
- Profile performance regularly

### Security
- Validate all inputs
- Sanitize user data
- Protect sensitive information
- Implement proper authentication
- Follow security best practices

### Testing
- Write unit tests
- Include integration tests
- Test error conditions
- Validate edge cases
- Maintain test coverage

### Documentation
- Document public APIs
- Include usage examples
- Document error handling
- Maintain changelog
- Update documentation with changes
